## Democracy and female representation 

Do democratic countries (`democ_regime == "Yes"`) have better female representation than non-democratic countries? Please answer this question by showing some graphs to assess the relationship between these two variables. 
library(dplyr)
library(ggplot2)

# Boxplot: compare the distribution of female representation
ggplot(data, aes(x = democ_regime, y = female_representation)) +
  geom_boxplot() +
  labs(
    x = "Democratic regime",
    y = "Female representation",
    title = "Female representation in democratic and non-democratic countries"
  )
# Bar graph: compare average female representation
data %>%
  group_by(democ_regime) %>%
  summarise(
    average_female_representation = mean(female_representation, na.rm = TRUE)
  ) %>%
  ggplot(aes(x = democ_regime, y = average_female_representation)) +
  geom_col() +
  labs(
    x = "Democratic regime",
    y = "Average female representation",
    title = "Average female representation by regime type"
  )
